Two edits in a GBEmulatorShootout checkout, both additive.

1) `main.py` — append to `EMULATOR_SPECS` (the list is in no particular order;
   the published table sorts by score):

    {
        'factory': lambda: _new_instance("emulators.terminalgb", "TerminalGB"),
        'keywords': ["TerminalGB", "terminalgb", "terminal-gb"],
        'name': "TerminalGB",
        'url': "https://github.com/Alchemy86/gameboy",
    },

2) `.github/workflows/ci-all.yml` — append to the `matrix.include` list:

          - emulator: TerminalGB
            needs_chromedriver: false
            needs_audio: true
            extra_requirements: ''

Notes:

* `keywords` are matched with `_normalize_emulator_keyword`, which lowercases
  and strips non-alphanumerics, so all three collapse to `terminalgb`. They are
  listed separately only so a reader can see which spellings are intended.
* The **repository slug is still `Alchemy86/gameboy`** — the product was
  renamed, the repo was not, and `downloadGithubRelease` takes the slug.
* The `title_check` in `emulators/terminalgb.py` matches the emulator's own
  window-title constant (`screen::desktop::WINDOW_TITLE`), which is a separate
  decision from this entry's display name. Changing one does not require
  changing the other.
